Source provenance

The following modules contain source extracted from the user's HomeCore
projects under the user's instruction to move their shared implementation
into Meerkat Toolkit:

  meerkat_toolkit/connectors/gmail_message.py
  meerkat_toolkit/frontend/inbox.py
  meerkat_toolkit/frontend/sender.py
  meerkat_toolkit/frontend/egress.py
  meerkat_toolkit/frontend/telegram.py
  meerkat_toolkit/frontend/telegram_adapter.py
  meerkat_toolkit/frontend/homecore_live.py
  meerkat_toolkit/_extension_wheels.py
  meerkat_toolkit/extension_artifacts.py

The inbox.py, sender.py and egress.py modules derive from HomeCore's existing
channel inbox and extension messaging owners. Exact captured source inventories and subsequent
changes are retained in the Toolkit repository under docs/reviews/ and
docs/coordination/20260930-upstream-review/frontend-egress-extraction/.
HomeCore has no root LICENSE, COPYING or NOTICE grant in the captured source.

The Telegram wire module derives from homecore-ext-telegram's provider.py at
f187bf89f49d4a0444fd3a9bffe07a49ab662f51. That project declares its license
as Private and has no root LICENSE, COPYING or NOTICE grant. TELEGRAM.md,
included alongside this file, describes the extraction and host boundary.
The exact source inventory is retained under
docs/coordination/20260930-upstream-review/telegram-frontend-transport-extraction/.

The Telegram provider adapter derives from the same private extension's
src/homecore_ext_telegram/extension.py, captured at SHA-256
79e41e310b63e92d63bd70f08abd5ae0cb28ef4cb798922f73f532b8a8157e42.
Its provider interpretation and presentation are separated from the host's
credentials, identity, admission, cursor and lifecycle owners. The exact
baseline and successor are recorded under
docs/coordination/20260930-upstream-review/telegram-frontend-adapter-successor/.

The HomeCore live image module replaces the send-image transport embedded in
homecore-reachy's src/reachyd/live.py at
0418a8b4e69a84f94adccd703a6060b9c293a49a. Its surrounding image job, lease,
channel and injection owners remain in HomeCore and Reachy. The inspected
Reachy root and extension have no LICENSE, COPYING or NOTICE file and no
declared package license. HOMECORE-LIVE.md, included alongside this file,
records that internal source relationship and its scope. Exact source and
dependency inventories are retained under
docs/coordination/20260930-upstream-review/reachy-image-transport-adoption/.

The Gmail message helper module derives from HomeCore's pure MIME composition,
reply linkage and readable-message interpretation in src/homecore/google_mcp.py,
captured at SHA-256
afa3902bf64b940d45ad3af10635896d9e176cb3fd6e5e2475160a38e51ffaaf.
The extraction separates generic formatting from HomeCore's HTML display and
account/admission/send owners, and adds explicit
malformed/incomplete decoding outcomes. No Google source code is copied. GMAIL.md
records the supported profile and ownership boundary. Exact donor and successor
files are retained under
docs/coordination/20260930-upstream-review/gmail-message-helpers-successor/.

The captured projects' private status and absent license files above describe
the extraction history. The grant at the top of this notice applies to the
listed Toolkit copies. Existing source attribution, copyright notices and
third-party license terms remain in place. Historical artifacts retain their
original notices and recorded identities.

No python-telegram-bot source is included in the Toolkit distribution. Toolkit's
optional telegram extra selects the existing python-telegram-bot==22.7 parser;
the HomeCore extension selects that extra. This separately distributed
dependency retains its LGPL-3.0-only metadata and existing license obligations.
